# Architecture constraints

{% callout type="info" title="About this chapter" %}
Constraints narrow the solution space before the first decision is made: requirements regarding technology, organization and conventions. Briefly note the background of each constraint.
{% /callout %}

## Technical constraints

| Constraint | Background |
|:---|:---|
| Runs on Kubernetes (Azure AKS) | Company-wide platform standard |
| Data stored in PostgreSQL | Existing operational experience, license costs |
| Mobile app for Android and iOS | Mixed device landscape across the fleet |
| Connection to SAP S/4HANA via the integration platform | Direct access to the ERP system is not permitted |

## Organizational constraints

- Go-live before the holiday peak season starts in November
- Two development teams of six people each, working in two-week iterations
- Operations and on-call duty provided by central IT Operations

## Conventions

- Architecture decisions are recorded as ADRs in [chapter 9](09-architecture-decisions.mdoc).
- Interfaces are described and versioned with OpenAPI 3.1.
- Code and documentation live together in the Git repository ("docs as code").
